node_modules
apps
# ...except the built browser game the game server serves at `/`.
!apps/assault-web/dist
# ...and the native client it serves at `/download/hAssault.exe`. Only `dist`:
# `apps/native-fps/target` beside it is tens of gigabytes of build cache.
!apps/native-fps/dist
# ...and the dashboard frontend the hosted hub serves at `/` (deploy/hub).
!apps/web/dist
packages
website
.git
.data
logs
*.log
.claude/worktrees
# Python build noise + local state that must not leak into the image.
**/__pycache__
.venv
*.db

# JVM heap/crash dumps (a Gradle OOM building apps/mobile-android drops a
# multi-hundred-MB java_pid*.hprof here). Already in .gitignore, but Docker does
# not read that file -- so without this they are uploaded to the builder on every
# deploy. One of them made the share-relay build context 853MB.
*.hprof
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log

# Module packages ship only their manifest and Python half (deploy/dashboard-node):
# the web half is bundled into the frontend, and tests never ship.
modules/*/web
modules/*/py/tests
